# Tri-platform build bar (ADR 0031): a clone must build identically on macOS,
# Linux, and Windows. Git-for-Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would
# check text files out with CRLF and byte-mangle the certified corpora, digests,
# and vectors that the project's own gates pin. `text=auto eol=lf` forces LF
# checkout on every platform; the byte-exact conformance trees are additionally
# marked -text so no eol attribute or future editor can ever touch them. The index
# is already all-LF, so introducing this file renormalizes nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf
priv/conformance/** -text
